{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"id\":\"U-ءخذ\",\"status\":\"reading\",\"finding\":\"In this surah, Form VIII اتخذ can establish a status or relation: a mosque over the sleepers, Satan as an ally, or misleaders as support. With حُسْنًا as its object and فِيهِمْ naming the people as its domain, the focus plausibly presents goodness as a chosen way of dealing with them—as policy, not a quality detached from governance.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"18:86\",\"ar\":\"وَإِمَّآ أَن تَتَّخِذَ فِيهِمْ حُسْنًۭا\"},{\"ref\":\"18:21\",\"ar\":\"لَنَتَّخِذَنَّ عَلَيْهِم مَّسْجِدًۭا\"},{\"ref\":\"18:50\",\"ar\":\"أَفَتَتَّخِذُونَهُۥ وَذُرِّيَّتَهُۥٓ أَوْلِيَآءَ\"},{\"ref\":\"18:51\",\"ar\":\"وَمَا كُنتُ مُتَّخِذَ ٱلْمُضِلِّينَ عَضُدًۭا\"}],\"activation\":\"The focus places تتخذ فيهم opposite تُعَذِّبَ as the other branch of a choice concerning قَوْمًا.\",\"limits\":\"The parallels establish taking on a role or relation, but do not decide whether the focus means kind treatment, beneficial governance, or a broader good course. The following verses specify outcomes by conduct without naming the precise policy.\",\"support\":\"strong\",\"relevance\":\"high\"}\n{\"id\":\"U-حسن\",\"status\":\"reading\",\"finding\":\"The unqualified حُسْنًا can name interpersonal good: 2:83 uses the same noun in the instruction to speak well to people. In the focus, فِيهِمْ and the contrast with تُعَذِّبَ activate that human-facing sense. The next verses make the good branch ethically selective: the wrongdoer is punished, while the believer who acts rightly receives جَزَاءَ ٱلْحُسْنَىٰ.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"2:83\",\"ar\":\"وَقُولُوا۟ لِلنَّاسِ حُسْنًۭا\"},{\"ref\":\"18:86\",\"ar\":\"وَإِمَّآ أَن تُعَذِّبَ وَإِمَّآ أَن تَتَّخِذَ فِيهِمْ حُسْنًۭا\"},{\"ref\":\"18:87\",\"ar\":\"أَمَّا مَن ظَلَمَ فَسَوْفَ نُعَذِّبُهُۥ\"},{\"ref\":\"18:88\",\"ar\":\"وَأَمَّا مَنْ ءَامَنَ وَعَمِلَ صَٰلِحًۭا فَلَهُۥ جَزَآءً ٱلْحُسْنَىٰ\"}],\"activation\":\"The focus applies حُسْنًا to a people and sets it beside punishment; the immediate continuation sorts the people by conduct and names the good branch’s reward.\",\"limits\":\"The parallel supports an interpersonal ethical sense but does not specify the ruler’s exact treatment. The distinct form ٱلْحُسْنَىٰ in 18:88 connects the passages without making the two forms identical in meaning.\",\"support\":\"strong\",\"relevance\":\"high\"}"}}
